4. Implement a `CircuitBreakerMonitor` class to track the number of consecutive failures and reset the circuit breaker when the threshold is exceeded (found in `CircuitBreakerMonitor.java`). This will ensure that the circuit breaker is properly reset after a certain period.

Example implementation:
```java
public class CircuitBreakerMonitor {
    private final int threshold;
    private final long timeout;

    public CircuitBreakerMonitor(int threshold, long timeout) {
        this.threshold = threshold;
        this.timeout = timeout;
    }

    public void monitor(CircuitBreaker circuitBreaker) {
        int consecutiveFailures = 0;
        long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

        while (System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime < timeout) {
            if (circuitBreaker.isBroken()) {
                consecutiveFailures++;
            } else {
                consecutiveFailures = 0;
            }

            if (consecutiveFailures >= threshold && circuitBreaker.isBroken()) {
                // Reset circuit breaker
                circuitBreaker.reset();
            }
        }
    }
}
```
